  "id": "Compound::DB00175 - Gene::28234",
  "verbalization": "Pravastatin, a widely used statin, exhibits a strong binding interaction with Slco2b1 and Slc22a6, which are both involved in the transport of organic anions across cell membranes. These transporters are functionally linked to Slco1b3, a gene that encodes a member of the Slco family of transporters. The evidence suggests that Pravastatin may modulate Slco1b3 through its interaction with these downstream transporters, potentially affecting bile acid and organic anion transport. The cumulative scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, with the strongest evidence pointing to the involvement of Slco2b1 and Slc22a6 in the transport process. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of anion transport, which could influence bile acid homeostasis and other physiological processes. While the exact functional role of Slco1b3 in this context remains to be fully elucidated, the integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Pravastatin and Slco1b3 through the regulation of anion transport activities.",
